**How to implement.** The test-scene default composes from the shipped files (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; .spec-md §3.4, §3.5). It is the composition the TestWindows heads and every `initMain ()` / `initTableAndElementRotation ()` fact run on. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, `module private DefaultStores`: `create ()` builds `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` (step 40) and runs `stores.proxy.importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` (steps 38, 40). On `Error e` it calls `Logger.logError` (`Softellect.Sys.Logging`, as `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs:155` does) with a one-line message carrying `e.describe`, and the scene starts with what was imported; nothing throws. `DefaultStoreSet` keeps its five fields: `materials`, `samples` and `categories` are the import's stores, `sources` is `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, and `library` is `liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources`. The `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go if nothing else needs them, and the module's doc says in at most three lines that it composes the scene's stores from the Built-in catalogue. (2) `CatalogueImport.fs`, `createInMemory`: the bundle's `libraryEntries` proxy answers the existing `By kind` grouping for `libraryTrees`, `(Library.createInMemory ()).libraryTrees` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemory`), whose leaves name the built-ins' frozen ids, so the Select bay's rows (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, `libraryState` over `model.library.libraryTrees ()`) are unchanged; its `entriesForKind` and `tryGetEntry` stay the import's. One doc line says so, and no other grouping is built here. Preset order now follows the catalogue's rows; the Select bay (tree order) and the Library window (`LibraryWindowView.fs:sortNodesByLabel`) do not show it, and no ordering is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs` gains `the default test scene composes its stores from the Built-in catalogue`: over `initMain ()`, `samples.listSamples IncludeInactive` holds exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()` by id, `materials.listMaterials IncludeInactive` exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`, `categories.listCategories ()` exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`, and `library.tryGetEntry` resolves every `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()` entry to itself.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, constructor-unit-tests and ui-smoke MUST pass, and ui-tests MUST pass over every class that composes the default test scene, including `the default test scene composes its stores from the Built-in catalogue` and LibraryControlsTests' Select-bay facts; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.
